-### 17.2 Formal Bearish ↔ Bullish mirror checklist
-
-| Concern | Bearish canonical behavior | Bullish counterpart | Non-directional guard |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| Physical Reaction First role | `FirstGreen` | `FirstRed` | Absolute timing, First/Break indices unchanged under sign reflection |
-| Confirm Reaction | strict `Low < BoxBottom` | strict `High > BoxTop` | Equality excluded; exact lower-TF confirmation eligible |
-| Reset Reaction / stop directional owner | strict `High > BoxTop` | strict `Low < BoxBottom` | Doji remains GREEN in both original market coordinate systems |
-| Scale Blue strike | increasingly higher `High`, confirmed RED | increasingly lower `Low`, confirmed GREEN | Break candle restricted to exact Reaction confirmation prefix |
-| Scale Blue level | `BoxBottom + 0.618 * (reference-BoxBottom)` | `BoxTop - 0.618 * (BoxTop-reference)` | Price-sign transformation, no float |
-| Scale / Reset Blue display | `High-(High-Low)/3` / `High-(High-Low)/5` | `Low+(High-Low)/3` / `Low+(High-Low)/5` | Source candle and interval invariant |
-| A source extrema | maximum eligible `High` | minimum eligible `Low` | Freeze at Reaction confirmation; preserve tie policy |
-| S source candidate extrema | maximum eligible `High` | minimum eligible `Low` | Type-3/Type-4 last-on-equality where specified |
-| Opposite Order strict stop | `Low < OrderStop` | `High > OrderStop` | Physical Order identity, provenance, same-candle ownership invariant |
-| Order_B reset leg | `HH=max High` and strict `High>HH` | `LL=min Low` and strict `Low<LL` | Must respect reset then strict break and A-expiry TF candle |
-| E/StopAll priority | `S Blue < E Blue < S Red < E Red` | Same | Behavioral family, numbering and owner identity invariant |
-| Direct StopAll | armed `S/E Blue x2` → next eligible accepted `S Red` | Same | Decision event time controls eligibility; no direction-specific shortcut |
-
-**Doji caveat:** exact sign-inverted original market candle Doji remains GREEN on both sides; color swapping is valid only for strictly non-Doji candles. Runtime synthetic mirror fixtures exclude exact Doji at both lower/main timeframe so no intentional Doji asymmetry is mistaken for directional drift. Real RAW tests retain all original Doji unchanged.
